MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_001: Good work today, Rocinan. You should be proud.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_002: Hey, what's the matter? Shh... What is it?
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_003: Your horse is called Rocinan, right? I knew another\nhorse with that name once.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_004: See, it's only Tialla. Relax, boy... This isn't like you.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_005: This isn't Sir Sariff's horse by any chance, is it?
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_006: You speak of my late father. I inherited this beast\nfrom him when I was 15.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_007: Hm. How could you know my father and Rocinan?\nAre you familiar with the knights of Arago?
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_008: I knew it! I have met this horse, although it was\nquite a while ago.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_009: My parents were stationed in Grand Aragon, serving\nunder King Hasdrubal.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_010: Sir Sariff brought this horse to our house a few times.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_011: Father was a friend to many. Where did you live?
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_012: Mahón Castle. And now I'm recalling that he might\nhave had his son with him.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_013: That's right. You must have been in August's\nhousehold at that time.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_014: I left my country years ago. I never expected we'd\nmeet again in these circumstances.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_015: Me neither. And who'd have thought that little boy\nwould grow up to become a mercenary?
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_016: Indeed. Of course, I'm just as surprised to see that\nyou're a mage now.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_017: Then again, your mother had a great talent for magic,\ndidn't she? So it makes sense.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_018: Io, you seem to have a way with that horse. I guess\nyou inherited that from Sir Sariff too.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_019: M-maybe so...
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_020: And you remembered me too, didn't you, Rocinan?\nSo nice to see you again.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_021: Io, do you mind if I pet your beautiful horse?
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_022: Not at all. I'm sure Rocinan would like that.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_C_023: {SetColor=Gray}Hmm... My father's legacy... But I'm still no\ngreat knight.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_001: Io, Rocinan, you're both safe. Excellent. Not that I'd\nexpect anything less.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_002: We've been together since I was born. We know\neach other's movements well.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_003: You inherited Sir Sariff's harmony with this horse,\nbut your fighting style is different from your father's.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_004: You've got those sly mercenary techniques, and you\naren't afraid to use them.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_005: I know—not very like the son of a knight.\nFather was always so calm in battle.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_006: I didn't mean it that way. It's just that you and Sir\nSariff are a study in contrasts.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_007: I tend to notice these things because they often\nimpact the strategies I develop.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_008: It's part of my job, really, developing battle plans\nbased on the characteristics I see in people.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_009: That's admirable work. Your parents must be proud.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_010: You too, Io. You may be a mercenary, but you have a\nknight's sensibilities.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_011: When we met as children, I must have been 6,\nwhich would mean you were about 10.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_012: Our parents would be shocked if they could see us\ntogether now. "Look at our brave kids!"
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_013: I may not be a knight like Father yet, but I promise\nto see you home alive.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_014: I owe it to your parents too. They were kind to me.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_015: So chivalrous all of a sudden.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_016: I do my best. I'm not there yet, but one day I'll be a\ntrue knight.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_017: Friends who fight together have to look out for each\nother, right?
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_018: I'm sure our parents treated each other that same\nway when they served King Hasdrubal.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_019: Just bear in mind that I don't need protection.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_020: We stand together as equals on the battlefield, Io.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_021: Of course. Your abilities speak for themselves.\nYou wield your mother's magic with ease.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_022: You better believe it. In any fight, I've got you\ncovered.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_023: {SetColor=Gray}But I can't help but want to protect you, Tialla.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_024: {SetColor=Gray}We've known each other since we were little, and\nyou've grown into such an impressive woman.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_025: Has your face gone red? Better let me know if\nyou're ill. It'll affect my tactics.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_026: Oh, no. It's nothing. I'm just, uh, moved is all.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_027: I once saw you clinging to your mother's leg, and\nnow look how far you've come.
MID_SE_Tia_Iio_B_028: Hey, go easy on the embarrassing childhood\nmemories!